From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 08:56:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Detect lines: one line record per printed line inside
 text regions

- app/services/lines.py: ink bands inside the region box (gray < 140,
  height >= 12 px, gaps <= 4 px merged, 6 px pad, clipped to the region),
  matched in order to the region's text lines. Texts come from the region
  text split at newlines, else from its current lines (saved region text is
  space-joined). Heading '#' markers are ignored; form fields get
  label/value roles. On a count mismatch one line is kept and a warning is
  returned. Only the processed regions' non-table lines are replaced.
- POST /documents/{id}/detect-lines {doc?, element_id?} -> {record, warnings}
- Right panel: 'Detect lines: page' and 'Selected region', warnings listed

